<title>NETHERLANDS: ROOD TESTHOUSE 1996 NET PROFIT DIVES.</title>
<headline>ROOD TESTHOUSE 1996 NET PROFIT DIVES.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     0.02 vs   0.61 </p>
<p>    Net profit			     0.16 vs   3.69</p>
<p>    Turnover			     107.9  vs 122.17</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     3.03 vs   3.61</p>
<p>    Interest charges		     1.65 vs   0.52 gain</p>
<p>    Tax					1.28 vs   0.12</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items	   gain 0.06 vs   0.56 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is Rood Testhouse NV. The electronic chip</p>
<p>testing firm said last June it would not realise its previous</p>
<p>forecast of higher earnings per share in 1996 because the</p>
<p>recovery at its French unit was taking longer than anticipated.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
